{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgdYxJULkj4bGVsZeFPAM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"OpenAI has committed to publishing a Community Safety Report every six months, with the first due in early 2027 and covering the second half of 2026. The company says it will explain how it trains systems to detect, investigate, and respond to community safety issues, share anonymized examples of how violence-related harm appears, highlight new mitigations and policy changes, and include relevant data supporting its findings. The report is framed as a way to show how well the safeguards work as well as what they are.\n\nThe only figure in the announcement so far is that OpenAI made over 200 law enforcement referrals in the third quarter of 2026 for imminent threats of violence. The company says these referrals are making a positive difference in disrupting violent plots, and that it relies on mental health and behavioral experts to assess difficult cases. That account is OpenAI's own. The announcement gives no count of plots disrupted, no description of what happened after referrals, and no figure for how many conversations were reviewed to produce them, so the number on its own is hard to interpret.\n\nThe first report will cover a period that includes that third quarter, which makes a direct comparison possible if the report uses the same measure. The announcement does not say whether it will, or which other statistics will appear beyond the phrase \"relevant data.\" Whether the six-month cadence produces a usable trend depends on the company keeping its definitions stable from one report to the next, which is an open question rather than a stated commitment.\n\nOpenAI also describes AI companies as having a distinct role alongside law enforcement, family members, mental-health professionals, and policymakers, who it says bring authority, context, and real-world reach. The referral figure and the reports are the two places where the public will be able to see how that division of work operates in practice."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":947,"cache_read_input_tokens":7507,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":947},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"16675d8d-fb07-4158-9574-927ab2753178","uuid":"f8900de3-fc52-43dc-ae4d-dfa99c32d38c","timestamp":"2026-11-02T05:30:27.546Z","request_id":"req_011CgdYxJGC7EafX7FdHjohW"}
